<title>USA: Kaman wins $600 mln Australian contract.</title>
<headline>Kaman wins $600 mln Australian contract.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMFIELD, Conn. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kaman Aerospace International Corp said Thursday it has signed a contract worth $600 million to supply helicopters and support for the Australian Ministry of Defence.</p>
<p>The company said the order calls for 11 SH-2G(A) Super Seasprite helicopters and support for the Royal Australian Navy.</p>
<p>The helicopters will operate from eight ANZAC class frigates, the company said. Their primary role is to provide expanded surveillance capabilities, but they will also be used for antisubmarine operations, search and rescue missions, medical evacuations and ship replenishment.</p>
</text>
